course: dictionary
lesson: 8323
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word rocky can mean covered with rocks, shaky, or full of problems. «The Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes, which give them shade and a lookout.» Here rocky means made of rock, because the outcrops are hard stone that the lions climb onto.
explain: «The rocky table wobbled every time Mia wrote, so she folded a card under one leg.» A table cannot be covered with rocks, so rocky must mean not steady. The clues are wobbled and folded a card under one leg. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «Ben's new school got off to a rocky start, with a lost bag and a late bus.» A lost bag and a late bus are problems, so rocky here means difficult. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Rocky means covered with rocks or made of rock, like a rocky beach or rocky hills.
fact: Rocky can also mean shaky or not steady, like a rocky table.
fact: Rocky can mean difficult and full of problems, as in «a rocky start».
fact: Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars are the rocky planets; the others are gas or ice giants.
fact: Rocky paths and wet rocks are slippery, so wear good shoes and watch where you step.
exercise: «The Earth has a thin rocky crust, a thick hot mantle and a very hot core in the middle.» What does rocky mean here? | *Made of rock | Shaky and not steady | Smooth and shiny | Difficult, with problems
exercise: Mia says her table is rocky because it wobbles when she writes. What does rocky mean? | Very old | Covered with rocks | Difficult, with problems | *Shaky or not steady
exercise: «Ben's new school got off to a rocky start, with a lost bag and a late bus.» What does rocky mean here? | Covered with rocks | Smooth and shiny | Quiet and calm | *Difficult, with problems
test: Which of these is a rocky planet? | Neptune | Jupiter | *Mars | Saturn
test: Why should you wear good shoes on a rocky path? | *Because rocky paths and wet rocks are slippery | Because shoes make rocks grow | Because rocky paths are always dry | Because rocky paths are soft and warm
exam: Which sentence uses rocky to mean shaky? | «The rocky hills rose above the sea.» | *«The rocky table wobbled, so we put a card under one leg.» | «We swam in the rocky pool all afternoon.» | «Our rocky holiday was full of sunshine.»
